\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{A cosmos comparison is optional later work. Specify the enriched model, limits, isofibrations, and module construction precisely, then compare its homotopy 2-category with a proved part of \code{Vert₂} or a suitable module equipment.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Existing formal machinery may help once its hypotheses have been ported.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Assuming a cosmos or its homotopy equipment comes for free from the root.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-ft-0009}, newly stated with exact scope before implementation.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{later (\ref{ms-0007}+).}
  \p{\ref{at-ft-0001} through \ref{at-ft-0007} remain proposed comparison tests with the revised scopes above. \ref{at-ft-0008}'s former arbitrary-root claim is retired. \ref{at-ft-0009} remains later. \ref{oq-ft-0001} is now the exact coherent restriction/unit transcription. \ref{oq-ft-0002} is which specific homotopy-equipment comparisons repay their construction cost; none is mandatory for the direct coherent route.}
}
